4.1 app/
It serves as the routing and core view layer for the frontend application. It defines the path users can viit
and handles the major e-commerce and user account functionalities.

Global Configuration
layout.tsx- the global layout for the application. It typically handles UI elements like footers and navbar

page.tsx- The main entry point or landing page for the application

global.css & favicon.ico: Handles the global styling rules and browser tab icons respectively

Ecommerce Funnel
categories/[category]- Dynamically lists products belonging to specific categories

products/[id]- It is a dynamic route for individual product landing pages and it fetches and displays detailed 
information for a single product

checkout- handles where users review their carts, enter shipping details and finalize possible payments.

User Management
profile- The user dashboard or user management page when logged in. They can likely view their details, 
order history and update settings.

verify email- Manages account security and email verification.

4.2 components/
They are isolated pieced of the user interface that can be plugged into various pages. This folder contains modular, reusable building blocks.

Navigation & Layout Elements
navbar.tsx and menu.tsx- the main navigation bar that holds the logo the user icon and the cart trigger.
It also handles responsive mobile menus, and site-wide routing links.

E-Commerce & Shopping Experience
cartDrawer.tsx- it lets users to see their selected items, adjust quantities and proceed to checkout without leaving their current page

FeaturedProducts.tsx- It is a specialized grid used on the landing page to highlight top-selling, discounted,  or new-arrival items.

ProductDisplay.tsx- Used for showing individual product cards

ProductsClient.tsx-Manages interactive client-side logic for product grids, including filtering, sorting, and pagination

Marketing & Engagement
Hero.tsx- It renders the primary marketing banner and Call-to-Action on the landing page


4.3 context/
The context folder utilizes the React Context API. Instead of passing down through multiple levels of components via 
props these files create global data stores. components can plug directly into these contexts to read or update data instantly

AuthContext.tsx- Manages global user authentication states

CartContext.tsx- Powers the e-commerce shopping engine and maintains the real-time state of items in the shopping cart


4.4 public/
in the public folder acts as the static asset storage for the application. Files within this folder are mapped directly to the root of the 
application server which allows them to be referred globally using absolute paths without build-step bundling.

4.5 package.json
The `package.json` file serves as the definitive manifest for the frontend application, managing third-party packages, system scripts, and project metadata.

